<header><p class="st-kicker">tribal confederation · Balkans and Hungary</p><h1 class="st-title">Moesi</h1><p class="st-meta">300 BCE – 29 BCE (approx.)</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">Thracian people of the Danube plain who gave their name to the Roman province of Moesia.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>Known mainly from Roman sources, the Moesi lived along the right bank of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/danube">Danube</a> in modern <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/serbia">Serbia</a> and northern <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/bulgaria">Bulgaria</a>, probably related to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mysia">Mysians</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/asia-minor">Asia Minor</a>. They appear as a distinct people from the late centuries BCE.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>Little is recorded of their institutions. They lived in tribal communities of farmers and herders in the valleys south of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/danube">Danube</a>, neighbours of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/triballi">Triballi</a> and the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/scordisci">Scordisci</a>, and resisted Roman advances from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/macedonia-region">Macedonia</a>.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/marcus-licinius-crassus">Marcus Licinius Crassus</a> defeated them in his campaign of 29 BCE, and their land was organised as the province of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/moesia">Moesia</a> early in the 1st century CE. The province became a key <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/danube">Danube</a> frontier with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/legion">legionary</a> bases at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/belgrade">Singidunum</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/viminacium">Viminacium</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/novae">Novae</a>.</p><p class="st-conf">Few sources survive for this state; details are uncertain.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="tribal confederation, 300 BCE – 29 BCE (approx.)"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><ellipse cx="44" cy="56" rx="16" ry=